---
// src/pages/dedicated-servers.astro
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="Dedicated Bare Metal Servers Sourcing | InfraHub"
  description="Source single-tenant bare-metal enterprise servers across Europe, North America, and Asia. High-bandwidth unmetered ports, NVMe storage, and AMD EPYC / Intel Xeon processors."
  canonicalPath="/dedicated-servers"
>
  <div class="section section-hero network-overlay">
    <div class="container service-container">
      <div class="service-header">
        <div class="header-badge-row">
          <span class="pill-badge badge-blue">Infrastructure</span>
          <span class="pill-badge badge-teal">Partner Sourced</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="service-title">Dedicated Bare Metal Infrastructure</h1>
        <p class="service-lead">
          Procure high-performance, single-tenant physical servers without noisy neighbors, virtualization overhead, or unpredictable cloud billing. Sourced across Tier-III facilities in Europe, Asia, and the Americas.
        </p>
        <div class="service-hero-actions">
          <a href="/lets-talk?service=dedicated-servers" class="btn btn-accent btn-lg">Request Server Configuration</a>
          <a href="/offers" class="btn btn-secondary btn-lg">View Live Stock Offers</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="content-section">
        <span class="section-sub-tag">Workload Performance</span>
        <h2>Why Pure Bare Metal Outperforms Hyperscaler Cloud</h2>
        <div class="problem-grid">
          <div class="problem-card">
            <h3>100% Dedicated Hardware</h3>
            <p>Direct access to raw CPU instructions, hardware virtualization extensions, and NVMe controller queues with zero hypervisor jitter.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="problem-card">
            <h3>Unmetered Bandwidth</h3>
            <p>Bare-metal providers may offer high-capacity or unmetered network options that can be easier to budget than usage-based cloud egress. Exact port speeds, commits, and traffic terms vary by provider.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="problem-card">
            <h3>Custom Hardware Profiles</h3>
            <p>Match processor generation, memory density, storage layout, and network interfaces to the workload instead of assuming one standard server profile.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="content-section">
        <div class="infrahub-role-card">
          <span class="pill-badge badge-teal">Global Sourcing</span>
          <h2>Ecosystem Providers: Zenlayer, Gcore & Limestone</h2>
          <p>InfraHub can compare bare-metal options from regional and global operators, including hardware, network, location, support, and commercial terms.</p>
          <div class="role-points-grid">
            <div class="role-point">
              <h3>Frankfurt & Amsterdam</h3>
              <p>Ultra-low latency to European eyeball networks with direct DE-CIX and AMS-IX peering routes.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="role-point">
              <h3>Singapore & Hong Kong</h3>
              <p>Regional network reach varies by facility and provider; compare actual routing, carrier mix, and latency to the markets that matter to the workload.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="role-point">
              <h3>Ashburn & Dallas</h3>
              <p>Massive domestic North American transit blending with carrier-neutral cross-connect flexibility.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="service-footer-cta">
        <h2>Source Dedicated Servers for Your Workload</h2>
        <a href="/lets-talk?service=dedicated-servers" class="btn btn-accent btn-lg">Request Dedicated Sourcing</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .service-container { max-width: 1040px; }
  .service-header { text-align: left; max-width: 860px; margin: 0 0 64px; padding-bottom: 24px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color); }
  .header-badge-row { display: flex; justify-content: flex-start; gap: 8px; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .service-title { font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4vw, 3.4rem); font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.15; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .service-lead { font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.65; margin-bottom: 32px; }
  .service-hero-actions { display: flex; justify-content: flex-start; gap: 14px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .content-section { margin-bottom: 72px; }
  .section-sub-tag { display: block; font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: var(--accent-blue); margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .content-section h2 { font-size: 1.85rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 18px; }
  .problem-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 20px; }
  @media (min-width: 768px) { .problem-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); } }
  .problem-card { background-color: var(--bg-secondary); border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 24px; }
  .problem-card h3 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 10px; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .problem-card p { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.5; }
  .infrahub-role-card { background-color: var(--bg-dark); color: #ffffff; border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 44px 36px; }
  .infrahub-role-card h2 { color: #ffffff; margin: 12px 0 16px; }
  .infrahub-role-card > p { color: var(--text-on-dark-muted); font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 32px; }
  .role-points-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 24px; }
  @media (min-width: 768px) { .role-points-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); } }
  .role-point { background-color: transparent; border: none; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12); border-radius: 0; padding: 18px 0 0; }
  .role-point h3 { color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .role-point p { color: var(--text-on-dark-muted); font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .service-footer-cta { padding: 40px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; text-align: left; gap: 16px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color); }
</style>
